id: pm-publication-acceptance-fence
title: Prevent exact-tag recovery from republishing an accepted npm version while public metadata is unavailable
description: "Actual Release38107714902 accepted signed npm2026.10.11 at03:45:06UTC while anonymous metadata and tarball remained404 at04:15. Existing Select exact-tag recovery source treats E404 as unpublished and permits first publication from the tag without inspecting earlier successful Publish to npm steps. Preserve existing exact tag/source identity and registry gating; introduce authoritative prior-publication admission before the checkout changes."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T04:17:35.484Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T05:49:39.468Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-11T05:49:38.669Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-11T05:49:38.669Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "Anonymous E404 after an authoritative successful same-tag Publish to npm step refuses first-publication recovery before checkout or gates; all prior matching run attempts are inspected; unrelated tags, workflows or branch identities cannot certify accepted publication; unavailable or malformed provider evidence refuses; genuinely never-published exact-tag recovery remains supported; actual failed daily run is independently replayed."
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: "Deliver complete paginated authoritative publication admission, portable native provider isolation and exact source coverage. Consolidate duplicated recovery documentation while preserving all operating contracts and immutable source/publication safeguards."
expected_result: "Accepted or incomplete evidence refuses publication, complete evidence supports guarded exact-tag recovery, and the full documented artifact remains within unchanged size limits."
actual_result: 59 linked release regressions and exact full5ed-source100percent coverage pass; real paginated provider replay refuses accepted11. Final documentation build/artifact/docs checks and unchanged HTTP regression replay pass. Prior91-byte artifact excess and native Windows readiness observation are retained; fresh final-head hosted checks and full review remain required.
